Dear Sir/Madam,

I am writing to formally register a complaint regarding the persistent lack=
 of substantive response and engagement from the Employment Tribunal concer=
ning my ongoing case.

I raised my first requests in February, it is now June and the tribunal has=
 yet to properly acknowledged my request whilst issues new orders.

The email below sent on the 30th of May 2025 has not had a response. I prov=
ided a 14 days deadline for a response and have not received one. The deadl=
ine has passed.

The respondent in this matter continues to demonstrate a clear failure to a=
dhere to even the most recent orders and persists in providing misleading i=
nformation. The respondent's actions have ruined the process's integrity an=
d continue to insult it. The absence of punishment and deterrent from the t=
ribunal has worsened the respondent's and Pinsent Masons LLP's conduct.

Their latest tactic: hiding Mr. Ride's UTR, claiming the comparator lacked =
one. I exposed the lie, and suddenly it 'appeared.' They're tampering with =
evidence, and the tribunal is doing nothing.

I consider the Employment Tribunal to be failing in its duties to ensure a =
fair and just process. This email serves as a formal complaint against the =
Tribunal's handling of this matter.
It is my understanding that, as per legal requirements, I must exhaust all =
available options with the Tribunal before escalating this matter. Therefor=
e, I intend to raise these concerns with the Equality and Human Rights Comm=
ission (EHRC) at the earliest opportunity provided by law, should this situ=
ation not be rectified promptly.

I respectfully request that the Tribunal either addresses these matters wit=
h the urgency and diligence they require or, if it deems itself unable to d=
o so, escalates the case to a higher court. I do not believe a fair trial i=
s possible due to the actions of the respondent and their solicitors and be=
cause the employment tribunal has allowed this.

Kind regards,
Abdul Alim

